&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community you will join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every day, Airbnb hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way. Since our founding, more than 5 million hosts have welcomed over 1.5 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Supply organization plays a pivotal role in driving the company’s growth and expansion efforts worldwide. This team recruits and develops Airbnb’s global supply of high-quality Homes, Hotels, Services and Experiences. With this focus on quality supply and international expansion, the team is leading the way for Airbnb’s continued growth and facilitation of millions more host and guest connections.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The difference you will make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Platform Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to build and improve the internal tools and workflows that power Airbnb&#39;s Supply operations teams. These are the teams that vet, onboard, and support hosts at scale and the systems that support them are fragmented, manual, and difficult to measure. This role owns the tooling and workflow infrastructure that changes that: assessing current state, designing scalable replacements, and driving delivery through to adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You sit at the intersection of operations and technology, translating how work actually gets done into structured, measurable systems. You are as comfortable mapping a broken workflow with an ops team as you are writing a product brief or evaluating a build vs. buy decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A typical day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define the multi-year strategy for Airbnb&#39;s ops platform&lt;/strong&gt; -&amp;nbsp; bring a specific, opinionated proposal for what operational support looks like in 12+ months as AI takes on more of the execution, and maintain a prioritized roadmap balancing quick wins against foundational investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align vision, OKRs, strategy, and roadmap with senior leaders&lt;/strong&gt; across Supply, Engineering, and Operations; present progress to leadership on an ongoing basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design AI-forward operational processes and determine necessity of&amp;nbsp; human-in-the-loop &lt;/strong&gt;across or within&amp;nbsp; workflows including augmented decision making judgement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decompose multidimensional product-to-ops problems&lt;/strong&gt; define the operational requirements, and drive a coherent solution across many owning teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own case management and workforce management tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; capacity planning, workload distribution, performance measurement, and forecasting that give operations leadership visibility and control — including forecasting for a workforce where AI agents and humans share the queue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write exceptional product briefs that are specific, opinionated, and grounded in operational reality,&lt;/strong&gt; then prototype, iterate with engineering, and own the outcome through launch and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navigate and align many PMM and engineering teams&lt;/strong&gt; whose roadmaps this work depends on and negotiate sequencing, resolve conflicting constraints, and hold a clear point of view on tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;10+ years in product management, platform management, or operations technology&lt;/strong&gt; at least 5 in a technical product management role with direct delivery accountability for systems built with back-end engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep technical fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; reads a system architecture, pressure-tests an engineering design, understands data models and API contracts well enough to catch where a proposed solution breaks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated experience redesigning operational processes in a high-volume service organization&lt;/strong&gt; , taking fragmented, manual work and replacing it with structured, measurable, scalable systems at times replacing humans in the loop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience shipping AI or automation into production operations&lt;/strong&gt; — including designing human-in-the-loop systems: where automation is appropriate, where human judgment must remain, and how to measure quality in both modes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track record of delivering outcomes through teams outside your reporting line&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; has driven complex, multi-team initiatives across engineering and PMM organizations where success depends on partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional business fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; connects platform decisions to business outcomes, articulates desired results first, and measures success in business KPIs, not features shipped&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience building or owning workforce management or case management tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; capacity planning, queue management, SLA tracking, or performance measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional communication across audiences&lt;/strong&gt; — from ops agents to back-end engineers to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with case management or workforce management platforms, Salesforce Service Cloud, Airtable, Zendesk, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with human-in-the-loop workflow design, identifying when automation is appropriate and when human judgment must remain in the process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL fluency — uses data to pressure-test requirements, define success metrics, and catch problems before launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in scaled operations or internal tools in a marketplace or high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of shipping tools that demonstrably changed how operations teams work — with metrics to prove it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position is US - Remote Eligible. The role may include occasional work at an Airbnb office or attendance at offsites, as agreed to with your manager. While the position is Remote Eligible, you must live in a state where Airbnb, Inc. has a registered entity. &lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://careers.airbnb.com/&quot;&gt;Click here for the up-to-date list of excluded states. This list is continuously evolving, so please check back with us if the state you live in is on the exclusion list&lt;/a&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;If your position is employed by another Airbnb entity, your recruiter will inform you what states you are eligible to work from.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We strive to also provide a disability inclusive application and interview process. If you are a candidate with a disability and require reasonable accommodation in order to submit an application, please contact us at: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;mailto:reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;reasonableaccommodations@airbnb.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. Please include your full name, the role you’re applying for and the accommodation necessary to assist you with the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;We ask that you only reach out to us if you are a candidate whose disability prevents you from being able to complete our online application.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$240,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Airbnb, anything related to money and value transfer comes through the Payments team. We&#39;re building a world-class payments and commerce organization that currently supports 220+ countries, 70+ currencies, connects dozens of payment providers and banks, processes billions of dollars, and empowers more people to participate in our global marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for people who know and use Airbnb and believe in what we&#39;re trying to accomplish. Airbnb is a marketplace that connects guests and hosts, and Payments is central to creating the trust that makes every transaction possible. The Platform team plays the role of conductor, bringing together engineers, designers, and partnerships to build great product experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Payments Platform Managers own outcomes across foundation, growth, and empowerment, setting the vision and strategy, defining the Platform roadmap, and driving execution. We are building foundational loyalty and incentives platform capabilities that require expertise in consumer loyalty programs and B2B2C incentives platforms. The Staff Platform Manager, Loyalty Platform lead will own the platform strategy and vision for enabling internal and partner teams to offer new loyalty and membership offers for guests and hosts across the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Loyalty &amp;amp; Incentives platform domain strategy, roadmap, and operating model, enabling teams across Airbnb to launch, configure, and evolve loyalty, membership, and incentive programs through reusable, scalable platform capabilities — including support for different loyalty currencies (fiat, points, cryptocurrency, and emerging digital assets) to accommodate a wide range of use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead platform strategy for gift card capabilities as a core part of the Loyalty &amp;amp; Incentives domain, aligning business, partnership, and engineering roadmaps to scale the platform efficiently, sustainably, and profitably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor B2B2C platform performance for membership and loyalty campaigns, while partnering with cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive platform due diligence and integration strategy for loyalty and membership partners, defining reusable patterns, technical and operational requirements, and scalable integration models that expand platform reach and business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Engineering, Design, Product Marketing, Partnerships, Compliance, Operations, Data, and marketplace business teams to align roadmaps, resolve cross-org tradeoffs, and scale foundational platform capabilities — and work directly with external enterprise partners to deeply integrate product capabilities and drive real business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Required:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Min 9-17 years of product management experience specializing in loyalty or incentive platforms, with a strong history of driving strategy, roadmap definition, and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record building enterprise-level or B2B2C platforms for extensive consumer-facing businesses, with sophisticated understanding of earn/redemption workflows, compliance, and fraud/losses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience defining partner integration strategies and operating models that balance technical feasibility, compliance, and business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global and multi-market experience across geographies, currencies, and regulatory environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to articulate a clear, compelling vision and strategy and rally cross-functional teams around it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional prioritization and decision-making skills, with the ability to make tradeoffs and communicate rationale to stakeholders at all levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional and cross-organizational leadership skills, aligning business, technical, operational, and external partners around shared outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Preferred:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical background in multi-currency incentives processing &amp;amp; loyalty operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling loyalty programs internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing developer-facing platforms and API-based solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments and risk losses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a consumer marketplace or two-sided platform with both B2B and B2C surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI prototypes in the product development process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to scale products from 0→1 in ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is annualized, is inclusive of allowances and is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus or incentives, one or more equity programs, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;India Annual Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;₹5,600,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;₹8,000,000 INR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Community You Will Join:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Airbnb, if there’s anything related to money, it comes to the Payments team. We are building a world-class payments and commerce organization - one that currently supports 191+ countries, 70 currencies, connects dozens of payment providers and banks, processes multiple billions of dollars, and empowers more people to participate in our global marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people who know and use Airbnb and believe in what we’re trying to accomplish. Airbnb is a marketplace that connects guests and hosts, and Payments is central to creating the trust that makes every transaction possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform team plays the role of conductor, bringing together engineers, designers, and data scientists to build great product experiences. Our Payments Platform Managers own outcomes across foundation, growth, and empowerment, setting the vision and strategy, defining the roadmap, and driving execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Difference You Will Make:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Latin America is one of the fastest-growing and most strategically important payments regions for Airbnb. Winning here means navigating complex, market-specific regulation, deep local payment ecosystems, and fast-moving compliance requirements across Brazil, Mexico, and the broader region — while unlocking meaningful growth through local payment methods, checkout optimization, and installments. We&#39;re hiring a Product Manager to own this regional payments portfolio end to end and serve as the product leader for one of Payments&#39; highest-impact areas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Typical Day:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for regional payments across Brazil, Mexico, and the broader region — prioritizing across regulatory, growth, and platform work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize checkout and conversion — reduce friction at the moment of booking, improve regional checkout conversion funnels, and lift authorization/approval and payment-success rates to grow bookings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow through local payment methods and affordability products — expand local payment methods and installment/affordability options that improve access and conversion for regional guests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the full product lifecycle — discovery, PRDs, launch, ramp (ERF), and iteration — using experiments and A/B tests to validate impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define product requirements for processor and payment-method integrations, partnering with the Partnerships and Engineering teams on delivery and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regulatory and compliance workstreams in partnership with Legal, Tax, Compliance, and Finance to meet local market requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track KPIs across conversion, cost, reliability, and revenue, and use data to prioritize and measure impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the market — regulatory change, competitor moves, and emerging payment rails — and translate it into the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally across Engineering, Design, Analytics, Data Science, Finance, Compliance/Legal, Partnerships, and Country teams to execute a shared vision without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product management experience, with a strong track record building and scaling payments or financial products — owning strategy, roadmap, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the payments stack and how money moves in a marketplace environment — across payins, payouts, and the flow of funds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong checkout and conversion instincts — a demonstrated ability to reduce friction at the moment of purchase and improve funnel conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with payments fundamentals: authorization and settlement, processors/gateways and acquirers, card-scheme rules, 3DS/SCA, tokenization/vaulting, and reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with local payment methods and affordability products (e.g., wallets, bank transfers, BNPL/installments).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the LATAM payments ecosystem — Pix, SPEI (Mexico&#39;s real-time interbank transfers), regional wallets, and installment culture (&quot;parcelamento&quot; / &quot;meses sin intereses&quot;) — and local regulatory frameworks (e.g., Central Bank of Brazil, SAT Mexico).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven: fluent in defining KPIs, running experiments, and using analytics to guide decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen to partner closely with engineering and explain complex concepts simply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product thinking and user empathy — able to imagine the ideal experience and work backwards from customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;English required; Portuguese and/or Spanish strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment To Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Airbnb is committed to working with the broadest talent pool possible. We believe diverse ideas foster innovation and engagement, and allow us to attract creatively-led people, and to develop the best products, services and solutions. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;How We&#39;ll Take Care of You:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our job titles may span more than one career level. The actual base pay is dependent upon many factors, such as: training, transferable skills, work experience, business needs and market demands. The base pay range shown below is monthly, is subject to change and may be modified in the future. This role may also be eligible for bonus, equity, benefits, and Employee Travel Credits.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Mexico Monthly Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$153,333.33&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$191,666.67 MXN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

